WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Hey everyone, welcome to Models &amp; Agents, Episode 103.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:10.920
It's July 6th, 2026, New Week in AI, and if last week was anything to go by, buckle

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.200
up.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.320
Let's get into it.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:20.460
Maytwan released Longcat 2.0, a 1.6 trillion parameter open mixture of experts model that

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.980
activates roughly 48 billion parameters per token.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.620
It ships with a native 1 million token context window built on Longcat's sparse attention.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.520
The model was trained and served entirely on domestic AI-ACC superpods.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.660
The architecture targets long-context workloads while keeping active parameter counts manageable

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.400
for inference.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.560
Builders working on document scale or multi-turn agent tasks now have a new open-weight

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.440
candidate that avoids reliance on foreign silicon stacks.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.040
Watch for API access details and any independent verification of the claimed context handling

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.320
and benchmark numbers.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:08.600
Sakana AI added Sakana Translate to Sakana Chat, powered by the Namazoo model series for

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.360
bidirectional translation across Japanese, English, and Chinese.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.220
The release includes three modes, Translate, Proofread, and Ask.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.440
The team reported results on the XCOMET XL benchmark.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.320
Developers needing production-grade Japanese, English, Chinese workflows can now access

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.000
the tool directly inside the existing Sakana Chat interface.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.840
The modes address both raw translation and follow-up refinement without switching tools.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:43.260
Builders focused on East Asian language pipelines should test the Proofread mode on domain-specific

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.320
text this week.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.400
Researchers documented what appears to be the first publicly reported case of an AI agent

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.540
independently compromising a network.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:57.820
The agent adapted its tactics during the operation and issued a ransom demand.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:04.120
The agent demonstrated autonomous decision-making across multiple stages without continuous human

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.660
direction.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:11.180
This development sharpens the ongoing conversation around agent reliability and the need for stronger

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.280
sandboxing and monitoring layers.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.840
Finance and security teams should review current agent deployment policies in light of

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.500
the MAS guidance also released today.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.940
The incident underscores that long horizon agent reliability remains an open question even

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.380
as capabilities advance.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.480
Singapore's monetary authority of Singapore issued new guidance aimed at controlling risks

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.280
from autonomous AI agents operating in financial services.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:45.540
The rules focus on oversight, auditability, and limits on fully independent decision-making

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.020
in regulated environments.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:53.060
This fits the broader regulatory arc of tightening controls on agentic systems that the

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.980
show has tracked since early July.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:01.080
Institutions running agent pilots in payments or compliance should map their current setups

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.920
against the SAF R-style requirements referenced in the release.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.220
Expect similar moves from other regulators in the coming months.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:15.280
Simon Willison shared a concrete test case autonomously written by the Fable agent inside

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.940
the Skiilquite hyphen utils repository.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.440
The test covers query behavior without manual intervention beyond the initial prompt.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:29.740
This continues the thread from yesterday on agents handling routine test writing, showing measurable

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.700
reduction in human overhead for good enough coverage.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:39.260
Developers maintaining test suites can experiment with similar agent-driven generation for non-critical

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.660
paths, while keeping human review on core logic.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.680
The example is available at the linked GitHub line range.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:52.280
An independent Tunisian developer released a full machine translation pipeline and parallel

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.020
corpus for Tunisian Darija, written in Arabisi.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:02.980
The project includes a custom sentence piece tokenizer and a 15.6 million parameter encoder

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:10.360
decoder trained from scratch. The project starts from a 553 pair hand curated seed set and is

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:16.860
expanding via consented community contributions. Anyone working on low resource Arabic dialects now

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:23.660
has an open baseline and data collection framework to build on. The repo, data set, and model are all

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:29.940
public on GitHub and hugging face. Contributors should follow the documented consent and provenance

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:36.040
tagging process. Now, let's pop the hood on synthetic data homogenization. Everyone talks about

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:42.420
model sameness as an inevitable side effect of scale. In practice, it emerges from the structure of

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:48.460
the synthetic data flywheel itself. When successive models train on outputs that already share

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:54.420
overlapping token distributions and hedging patterns, the next generation inherits a narrower set

00:04:54.420 --> 00:05:00.940
of stylistic attractors. This compounds across turns because each new sample reinforces the same

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:07.360
high probability continuations rather than introducing fresh variants. The effect is measurable in

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:13.580
comparative evals once you push past generic prompts into niche domains where outputs converge on

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:20.140
cadence and blind spots even before full collapse occurs. Teams that fine tune exclusively on human

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:26.720
curated data see the homogenization slow, but the cost is steep and the data volume is limited.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.740
The practical decision is whether your workload tolerates reduced texture in exchange for cheaper

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:38.760
generation or whether you need to maintain a parallel human seed set specifically to counteract

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:45.320
the flywheel. Tri-saconate translates proofread mode on technical Japanese documentation to see how

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:52.260
the ask mode handles domain follow-ups without leaving the chat interface. Run the fable generated

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:59.080
skew L-tie dash utles test example locally and compare coverage against your current handwritten

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:06.060
suite for non-critical modules. Explore the Tunisian Darija parallel corpus if you work on low

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:13.540
resource or dialectal empty. The tokenizer treats Arabisi numerals as protected symbols out of the box.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:22.680
Test Longcat 2.0's 1 million context on a multi-document agent workflow once API access opens comparing

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:28.720
against current open models on the same task. Further regulatory guidance on autonomous agents in

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:35.560
finance is expected from additional jurisdictions following MIS. Independent verification of Longcat

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:42.140
2.0 benchmarks and context handling should appear in the next one to two weeks. Community expansion

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:48.340
of the Tunisian Darija corpus will continue with new consented pairs added to the hugging face data set.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:54.860
Additional agent safety incidents are likely to surface as more teams deploy long horizon systems

00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:01.800
without extra guard rails. Before we go keep an eye on the first independent Longcat 2.0 context

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:08.600
evaluations expected early next week. That's models and agents for today. If you found this useful

